1
00:00:00,667 --> 00:00:01,633
<i> What were you thinking?</i>

2
00:00:01,767 --> 00:00:03,400
<i>The only way people
won't suspect anything,</i>

3
00:00:03,533 --> 00:00:07,833
<i>even if they recognize me,
is to show them I'm on vacation.</i>

4
00:00:07,967 --> 00:00:10,233
<i>I spoke with Joey.
He's with Andrew.</i>

5
00:00:10,367 --> 00:00:11,600
<i>They said they're
following a lead.</i>

6
00:00:11,733 --> 00:00:13,967
<i>Let's just follow Andrew.
We can help them too.</i>

7
00:00:14,100 --> 00:00:16,533
<i>Instead of getting closer,
I'll keep my distance.</i>

8
00:00:16,667 --> 00:00:17,900
<i>I'll just go home
to the province.</i>

9
00:00:18,033 --> 00:00:20,533
<i>I might not be able to take care
of this foundation for now.</i>

10
00:00:20,667 --> 00:00:23,667
<i> Mom lost her caregiver.</i>

11
00:00:23,800 --> 00:00:26,600
<i>Ma'am, if you can't find anyone,
I can help.</i>

12
00:00:26,733 --> 00:00:30,067
<i> If you agree,
it won't just be me helping you,</i>

13
00:00:30,200 --> 00:00:31,867
<i> you'll be helping me too.</i>

14
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:34,400
<i>Sir, the package was delivered
to Delgado.</i>

15
00:00:34,567 --> 00:00:36,267
<i>Hopefully that helps
his mission.</i>

16
00:00:36,400 --> 00:00:37,467
<i> Thank you, Chief.</i>

17
00:00:37,600 --> 00:00:38,600
<i> Whose is it?</i>

18
00:00:38,733 --> 00:00:41,400
<i>The guy in red,
we saw him in the other room.</i>

19
00:00:41,533 --> 00:00:43,600
<i> He called Delilah "boss."</i>

20
00:00:43,733 --> 00:00:46,200
<i>You're my ticket
to get close to Delilah.</i>

21
00:00:46,333 --> 00:00:49,167
<i>And if it's any help,
we confirmed Delilah is here.</i>

22
00:00:49,300 --> 00:00:50,600
<i>She's just in the room
next to us.</i>

23
00:00:50,733 --> 00:00:52,000
<i> I'm Madam Delilah.</i>

24
00:00:52,133 --> 00:00:52,967
<i> I'm Joey.</i>

25
00:00:53,100 --> 00:00:54,667
<i> We have camping areas.</i>

26
00:00:54,800 --> 00:00:55,933
<i>Don't worry,
I'll have it prepared.</i>

27
00:00:56,067 --> 00:00:58,267
<i> Too bad I have plans later.</i>

28
00:00:58,400 --> 00:01:00,933
<i>Castro said someone
asked about Berdugo.</i>

29
00:01:01,067 --> 00:01:04,033
<i>To avoid problems, I'll attend
the meeting with Delilah.</i>

30
00:01:04,167 --> 00:01:07,733
<i>She left, but I heard
she'll be back tonight.</i>

31
00:01:07,900 --> 00:01:09,133
<i> This is our chance.</i>

32
00:01:09,267 --> 00:01:10,633
<i> No one's at the villa.</i>

33
00:01:10,767 --> 00:01:12,567
<i> We can go in and find a clue.</i>

34
00:01:12,700 --> 00:01:14,600
<i>- Can you open that?
- Of course.</i>

35
00:01:14,733 --> 00:01:18,333
<i>Hello? I'm done cleaning.
I'm on my way there.</i>

36
00:01:20,467 --> 00:01:30,433
[OBB]

37
00:01:54,533 --> 00:02:04,500
[SENTIMENTAL MUSIC PLAYING]

38
00:02:08,900 --> 00:02:12,133
Yes, I'm on my way.
I'm coming, I'm coming.

39
00:02:12,267 --> 00:02:18,467
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

40
00:02:18,633 --> 00:02:28,600
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

41
00:02:34,133 --> 00:02:37,167
Boss, if you want, I'll get it
so you won't get tired.

42
00:02:37,300 --> 00:02:39,167
What do you need to get?

43
00:02:39,300 --> 00:02:40,833
My dear,

44
00:02:40,967 --> 00:02:42,167
I trust you but...

45
00:02:42,300 --> 00:02:44,867
I don't trust you enough
to give you personally

46
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:47,533
the combination of my safe.
I'll come back myself.

47
00:02:47,700 --> 00:02:48,833
Boys, let's go.

48
00:02:48,967 --> 00:02:53,400
[FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

49
00:02:53,533 --> 00:02:56,133
Just give it to Joey.
He might pass by.

50
00:02:59,400 --> 00:03:00,967
Okay.

51
00:03:01,100 --> 00:03:03,300
Are you sure about leaving?

52
00:03:03,433 --> 00:03:05,767
What about your work
with your uncle here?

53
00:03:05,900 --> 00:03:08,133
It's fine. I already told him.

54
00:03:08,267 --> 00:03:10,733
I'm needed back home,

55
00:03:10,867 --> 00:03:13,300
unlike here.

56
00:03:13,433 --> 00:03:16,100
What? Did I hear that right?

57
00:03:16,233 --> 00:03:18,467
You're leaving,
you're teasing me again.

58
00:03:18,600 --> 00:03:19,933
- Teasing?
- You're leaving

59
00:03:20,067 --> 00:03:23,233
because Joey has forgotten you,
right?

60
00:03:23,400 --> 00:03:24,767
What? Admit it.

61
00:03:24,900 --> 00:03:26,000
- Come on.
- Admit it.

62
00:03:26,133 --> 00:03:28,233
Fine, I need to go.

63
00:03:28,367 --> 00:03:29,733
Take care here.

64
00:03:29,867 --> 00:03:30,767
Thank you so much.

65
00:03:30,900 --> 00:03:33,933
All right, friend.
Take care too.

66
00:03:34,067 --> 00:03:36,400
-Take care, friend.
-Take care.

67
00:03:36,533 --> 00:03:38,433
- Bye.
- Hey! You're really leaving?

68
00:03:41,100 --> 00:03:42,967
My god! It's okay.

69
00:03:43,100 --> 00:03:44,400
Okay.

70
00:03:44,533 --> 00:03:46,367
Why are you so red?

71
00:03:46,500 --> 00:03:47,600
Are you okay?

72
00:03:47,733 --> 00:03:49,067
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

73
00:03:49,200 --> 00:03:52,267
I thought we'd get caught.
Let's go!

74
00:03:52,400 --> 00:03:53,567
Okay.

75
00:03:57,533 --> 00:04:07,500
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

76
00:04:14,167 --> 00:04:15,700
You know what? Stay here.

77
00:04:15,833 --> 00:04:17,000
Okay? Wait for me.

78
00:04:17,133 --> 00:04:18,300
- I'll look for...
- You're leaving me here?

79
00:04:18,433 --> 00:04:20,100
- Yes.
- Really?

80
00:04:21,067 --> 00:04:22,933
Andrew!

81
00:04:23,067 --> 00:04:24,700
Andrew!

82
00:04:24,833 --> 00:04:28,567
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

83
00:04:28,733 --> 00:04:30,033
What?

84
00:04:30,167 --> 00:04:38,000
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

85
00:04:38,133 --> 00:04:39,333
Andrew!

86
00:04:39,467 --> 00:04:49,433
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

87
00:04:52,867 --> 00:04:56,967
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

88
00:04:57,100 --> 00:04:59,167
- All right. You two stay there.
- All right, Boss.

89
00:04:59,300 --> 00:05:09,267
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

90
00:05:11,167 --> 00:05:12,133
Andrew!

91
00:05:13,633 --> 00:05:15,833
Andrew, let me in.
You're starting to annoy me.

92
00:05:15,967 --> 00:05:23,800
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

93
00:05:23,933 --> 00:05:26,767
Joey! Joey, there's a safe here.

94
00:05:26,900 --> 00:05:28,667
Do you know the combination?

95
00:05:28,800 --> 00:05:30,167
How would I know?

96
00:05:30,300 --> 00:05:31,733
Try 1-2-3-4.

97
00:05:32,767 --> 00:05:35,167
1-2-3. I already tried that.
Still nothing.

98
00:05:35,333 --> 00:05:40,700
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

99
00:05:40,833 --> 00:05:42,633
Why won't you let me in?

100
00:05:42,767 --> 00:05:44,533
I might find a clue!

101
00:05:47,900 --> 00:05:50,933
Andrew, let's go!
Someone might see us here!

102
00:05:51,067 --> 00:05:52,633
[FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

103
00:05:52,767 --> 00:05:55,567
Andrew, someone might come!
Hurry up!

104
00:05:55,700 --> 00:06:05,667
[FOREBODING MUSIC CONTINUES]

105
00:06:07,400 --> 00:06:08,800
Andrew...

106
00:06:10,467 --> 00:06:11,733
Andrew!

107
00:06:19,233 --> 00:06:20,500
Joey?

108
00:06:21,967 --> 00:06:23,100
What are you doing there?

109
00:06:23,233 --> 00:06:33,200
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

110
00:06:36,567 --> 00:06:37,733
It hurts!

111
00:06:37,867 --> 00:06:39,133
Awww!

112
00:06:39,267 --> 00:06:40,600
- Miss!
- Ouch!

113
00:06:40,767 --> 00:06:42,433
What happened to you?

114
00:06:42,567 --> 00:06:44,367
- Are you okay?
- No, I'm not!

115
00:06:46,333 --> 00:06:48,000
What happened
to you, ma'am?

116
00:06:49,833 --> 00:06:51,500
"Ma'am"?

117
00:06:51,633 --> 00:06:53,900
I'm not that old.

118
00:06:54,033 --> 00:06:55,733
I slipped!

119
00:06:55,867 --> 00:06:57,967
Because no one cleaned!

120
00:06:58,100 --> 00:06:59,933
Sorry, Miss...

121
00:07:00,067 --> 00:07:01,733
Zoey.

122
00:07:01,867 --> 00:07:03,833
Wait. Are you a guest here?

123
00:07:03,967 --> 00:07:06,267
Can you come with me to
see the resort manager?

124
00:07:06,400 --> 00:07:07,200
I'll file a complaint.

125
00:07:07,333 --> 00:07:08,767
I'll vlog about what
happened to me!

126
00:07:08,900 --> 00:07:12,633
Miss Zoey, Francis,
owner of the resort.

127
00:07:12,767 --> 00:07:16,900
You're right, it's our fault.

128
00:07:17,067 --> 00:07:18,300
Please accept our apology.

129
00:07:18,433 --> 00:07:21,067
So you're the owner?

130
00:07:21,200 --> 00:07:24,067
Miss Zoey, maybe we can talk...

131
00:07:24,200 --> 00:07:26,800
so we can fix this?

132
00:07:26,933 --> 00:07:31,033
If you want, your stay here
will be free of charge.

133
00:07:31,167 --> 00:07:34,133
Is that your best offer?

134
00:07:34,267 --> 00:07:35,600
FYI,

135
00:07:35,733 --> 00:07:39,800
I can pay for my accommodation
in this cheap resort.

136
00:07:39,933 --> 00:07:41,933
Miss Zoey, you're right.

137
00:07:42,067 --> 00:07:43,900
Our resort is very simple.

138
00:07:44,033 --> 00:07:47,300
But I'm sure you haven't tried
our amenities.

139
00:07:47,433 --> 00:07:48,933
We're very proud

140
00:07:49,100 --> 00:07:51,100
of our nature experiences
which you can try out.

141
00:07:52,367 --> 00:07:55,067
So, can I offer...

142
00:07:55,200 --> 00:07:57,033
dinner by the campsite?

143
00:07:59,800 --> 00:08:01,133
Wait, so...

144
00:08:01,267 --> 00:08:03,033
just me?

145
00:08:03,167 --> 00:08:04,933
You won't even join me?

146
00:08:06,800 --> 00:08:08,467
Don't worry, Miss Zoey. I'll
join you.

147
00:08:08,600 --> 00:08:12,800
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

148
00:08:12,933 --> 00:08:15,933
Why are you standing outside
my room?

149
00:08:22,400 --> 00:08:24,533
I'm looking for my boyfriend.

150
00:08:25,967 --> 00:08:29,767
You know what? When I see him,
he'll have to deal with me.

151
00:08:29,900 --> 00:08:31,267
I've had it with him.

152
00:08:31,400 --> 00:08:33,433
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

153
00:08:33,567 --> 00:08:35,800
Lover's quarrel.

154
00:08:35,933 --> 00:08:37,233
What happened?

155
00:08:37,367 --> 00:08:40,867
It seems that guy forgot
he's here with someone.

156
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:43,833
I just took a nap,
then he disappeared!

157
00:08:43,967 --> 00:08:45,933
Annoying, right?

158
00:08:46,067 --> 00:08:47,567
That's so sweet.

159
00:08:47,700 --> 00:08:51,500
You're so in love you
don't want to be apart.

160
00:08:51,633 --> 00:08:59,267
[UNEASY MUSIC CONTINUES]

161
00:08:59,433 --> 00:09:00,667
[THUDS]

162
00:09:01,733 --> 00:09:02,633
Look.

163
00:09:02,767 --> 00:09:04,233
[FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

164
00:09:15,533 --> 00:09:16,800
Check everywhere!

165
00:09:16,933 --> 00:09:26,033
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

166
00:09:26,167 --> 00:09:27,467
Check inside!

167
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:33,067
Maybe it was just the wind?

168
00:09:33,200 --> 00:09:34,233
It can't be.

169
00:09:34,367 --> 00:09:37,833
Look, all the doors and windows
are closed.

170
00:09:37,967 --> 00:09:47,933
[UNEASY MUSIC CONTINUES]
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

171
00:09:49,600 --> 00:09:59,567
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

172
00:10:00,800 --> 00:10:07,833
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

173
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:09,800
What? Did you see anything?

174
00:10:12,033 --> 00:10:13,300
Ma'am, there was nothing.

175
00:10:17,967 --> 00:10:20,400
Well, I guess you're right,
dear.

176
00:10:20,533 --> 00:10:22,200
Maybe it was just the wind.

177
00:10:26,600 --> 00:10:28,000
Oh, are you okay?

178
00:10:28,133 --> 00:10:29,933
You look scared.

179
00:10:31,833 --> 00:10:33,467
It's because of what sir
was holding.

180
00:10:33,600 --> 00:10:37,000
I'm not used to guns.
They're scary.

181
00:10:37,167 --> 00:10:38,433
Ah, is that so?

182
00:10:38,567 --> 00:10:40,333
Hey, put that away.

183
00:10:40,467 --> 00:10:42,300
You're scaring my neighbor.

184
00:10:43,433 --> 00:10:44,800
Sorry about that, dear.

185
00:10:44,933 --> 00:10:48,033
You know, these dayls,
you can't trust anyone.

186
00:11:00,333 --> 00:11:01,800
Are you sure you're okay?

187
00:11:03,633 --> 00:11:05,967
Sorry again for what you saw.

188
00:11:07,033 --> 00:11:08,700
It's fine.

189
00:11:08,867 --> 00:11:12,433
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

190
00:11:12,567 --> 00:11:14,733
Babe!

191
00:11:14,867 --> 00:11:16,667
What are you doing here?

192
00:11:18,433 --> 00:11:20,067
Where were you?

193
00:11:20,200 --> 00:11:21,300
I've been looking for you.

194
00:11:21,433 --> 00:11:23,300
I even called your mom

195
00:11:23,433 --> 00:11:27,367
to let her know that
we're having fun and we're safe.

196
00:11:27,500 --> 00:11:28,900
That's so sweet.

197
00:11:30,333 --> 00:11:31,700
Ma'am Delilah.

198
00:11:32,733 --> 00:11:34,133
I'm Andrew.

199
00:11:35,633 --> 00:11:37,167
You look familiar.

200
00:11:38,333 --> 00:11:41,267
Anyway, make up already,
you two.

201
00:11:41,433 --> 00:11:44,733
Don't waste your stay
at my resort

202
00:11:44,867 --> 00:11:47,867
over a small misunderstanding.

203
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:50,100
Thank you, Aunt Delilah.

204
00:11:50,233 --> 00:11:51,767
- Thank you.
- Aunt?

205
00:11:53,567 --> 00:11:55,667
Nobody has called
me that before.

206
00:11:57,467 --> 00:11:59,333
I kind of like it.

207
00:12:11,200 --> 00:12:13,500
[GROANS]

208
00:12:17,400 --> 00:12:19,200
You know what?
I feel so much better now.

209
00:12:19,333 --> 00:12:20,267
Thank you.

210
00:12:20,400 --> 00:12:22,600
- Did the pain subside?
- Yes, yes, thanks.

211
00:12:24,100 --> 00:12:29,600
So maybe we're now absolved
from that incident you had?

212
00:12:31,067 --> 00:12:36,700
You might post bad reviews
about our hotel on social media.

213
00:12:36,833 --> 00:12:39,633
Don't worry.
I'm not that kind of person.

214
00:12:39,767 --> 00:12:41,633
I won't do that.
Don't be afraid, okay?

215
00:12:41,767 --> 00:12:43,500
Really?

216
00:12:44,533 --> 00:12:46,100
Thank you then.

217
00:12:46,233 --> 00:12:50,033
We just want our resort
to stay quiet.

218
00:12:50,200 --> 00:12:54,833
Because if this gets posted
online and goes viral,

219
00:12:54,967 --> 00:12:56,367
it'll draw attention here.

220
00:12:56,500 --> 00:12:58,900
Then our resort
will become noisy.

221
00:12:59,033 --> 00:13:02,000
Even if you don't have
that many customers?

222
00:13:02,133 --> 00:13:04,867
What's important is the privacy
of our guests.

223
00:13:06,800 --> 00:13:08,133
Why?

224
00:13:08,267 --> 00:13:12,367
Do you have famous guests here?

225
00:13:12,500 --> 00:13:14,400
Powerful people?

226
00:13:14,533 --> 00:13:18,433
Or maybe criminal masterminds
are hiding here?

227
00:13:22,633 --> 00:13:24,333
Ouch...

228
00:13:24,467 --> 00:13:26,800
You're so dramatic.
But it's your fault.

229
00:13:26,933 --> 00:13:28,533
You left me, remember?

230
00:13:28,667 --> 00:13:30,333
I'm sorry, I'm sorry.

231
00:13:32,800 --> 00:13:36,433
But you know,
if you weren't outside earlier,

232
00:13:36,567 --> 00:13:38,133
I would've been caught.

233
00:13:38,267 --> 00:13:40,000
So...

234
00:13:40,133 --> 00:13:41,000
thank you.

235
00:13:41,133 --> 00:13:42,400
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

236
00:13:42,533 --> 00:13:45,300
Still.
You should've brought me inside.

237
00:13:45,433 --> 00:13:48,267
If I were there,
we might've found a clue.

238
00:13:49,933 --> 00:13:52,167
Never mind.
We still have a chance.

239
00:13:53,633 --> 00:13:55,433
Okay? Come on, I'm sorry.
Don't be mad anymore.

240
00:13:57,467 --> 00:13:58,700
[GROANS]

241
00:14:00,967 --> 00:14:03,567
- You even pressed harder.
- Stop moving.

242
00:14:08,567 --> 00:14:09,867
Thank you.

243
00:14:12,433 --> 00:14:15,733
By the way, you actually did...

244
00:14:15,867 --> 00:14:16,867
well earlier.

245
00:14:20,800 --> 00:14:22,667
Really?

246
00:14:22,800 --> 00:14:24,600
Yes.

247
00:14:24,733 --> 00:14:27,067
If not for your delaying
tactics,

248
00:14:27,200 --> 00:14:28,467
I would've been caught.

249
00:14:29,833 --> 00:14:34,400
And even though I know
you're annoyed with me,

250
00:14:34,533 --> 00:14:36,333
you didn't abandon me.

251
00:14:38,600 --> 00:14:40,267
Of course.

252
00:14:40,400 --> 00:14:44,367
It's not like I'd want anything
bad to happen to my boyfriend.

253
00:14:51,333 --> 00:15:00,233
[HEART POUNDING]
[ROMANTIC MUSIC PLAYING]

254
00:15:06,600 --> 00:15:09,133
[CHUCKLES]
Just kidding!

255
00:15:09,267 --> 00:15:11,133
Just kidding! Come on!

256
00:15:11,267 --> 00:15:12,533
I'm just like this.

257
00:15:12,667 --> 00:15:15,367
Hey, don't get annoyed with me,
okay? I'm just like this.

258
00:15:15,500 --> 00:15:17,433
This is just me.

259
00:15:17,567 --> 00:15:21,033
You might suddenly ditch me
at our dinner.

260
00:15:21,167 --> 00:15:23,867
7 PM, I'll pick you up.

261
00:15:25,167 --> 00:15:26,433
It's a date.

262
00:15:26,567 --> 00:15:30,267
[CURIOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

263
00:15:30,400 --> 00:15:32,233
Anyway, I'll go ahead.

264
00:15:32,367 --> 00:15:34,167
- All right.
- So, I'll see you?

265
00:15:35,633 --> 00:15:38,500
- 7 PM.
- Yeah. Bye!

266
00:15:45,433 --> 00:15:48,833
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

267
00:15:48,967 --> 00:15:51,933
We should stick
with our characters.

268
00:15:53,467 --> 00:15:56,533
Of course, we're pretending to
be boyfriend and girlfriend.

269
00:15:56,667 --> 00:15:58,367
So, we have to be consistent.

270
00:15:58,500 --> 00:16:01,567
No one should catch us,
no one should suspect anything.

271
00:16:02,767 --> 00:16:04,967
Right.

272
00:16:05,100 --> 00:16:06,400
You have a point.

273
00:16:08,200 --> 00:16:12,967
Maybe we shouldn't just
pretend in front of Delilah.

274
00:16:13,100 --> 00:16:15,267
We should pretend in
front of everyone.

275
00:16:15,400 --> 00:16:18,167
Because think about it,
we almost got caught earlier.

276
00:16:18,300 --> 00:16:20,400
Who knows? Next time, Delilah
might ask questions.

277
00:16:20,533 --> 00:16:25,300
[PLEASANT MUSIC CONTINUES]

278
00:16:25,433 --> 00:16:27,100
So...

279
00:16:27,233 --> 00:16:28,367
what do we do?

280
00:16:29,400 --> 00:16:33,267
Then we have to convince
everyone that...

281
00:16:33,400 --> 00:16:34,933
we really are together.

282
00:16:37,700 --> 00:16:39,500
I know. I have an idea.

283
00:16:39,633 --> 00:16:49,600
[ROMANTIC MUSIC PLAYING]

284
00:17:08,833 --> 00:17:09,833
[SPEAKS INDISTINCTLY]

285
00:17:09,967 --> 00:17:10,933
To the right.

286
00:17:11,067 --> 00:17:13,867
[WHOOSHING]

287
00:17:17,667 --> 00:17:18,500
90 degrees, right.

288
00:17:18,633 --> 00:17:25,633
[WHOOSHING]

289
00:17:25,767 --> 00:17:28,033
Can you still do it? Okay.

290
00:17:28,167 --> 00:17:29,367
Step forward.

291
00:17:30,533 --> 00:17:38,033
[WHOOSHING]

292
00:17:38,167 --> 00:17:48,133
[ROMANTIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

293
00:18:12,233 --> 00:18:16,467
[APPLAUDING]

294
00:18:16,600 --> 00:18:18,633
You two act so well.

295
00:18:18,767 --> 00:18:21,300
I would believe
you're really a couple.

296
00:18:21,467 --> 00:18:24,933
[ROMANTIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

297
00:18:25,067 --> 00:18:27,733
Zoey, I thought you don't want
your cover blown.

298
00:18:28,767 --> 00:18:29,267
Why are you here?

299
00:18:30,467 --> 00:18:32,567
Didn't you say we'd share info?

300
00:18:33,833 --> 00:18:35,267
Well, I just want
to let you know

301
00:18:35,400 --> 00:18:37,567
I have a date with Francis
tonight.

302
00:18:37,700 --> 00:18:40,733
This is my chance to
get closer to Delilah's circle.

303
00:18:40,867 --> 00:18:41,867
Great.

304
00:18:48,533 --> 00:18:51,900
Well, I guess that's good.
Good for you.

305
00:18:52,033 --> 00:18:54,867
But be careful,
just looking at Francis,

306
00:18:55,000 --> 00:18:56,733
I already don't trust him.

307
00:18:59,100 --> 00:19:01,600
You're worried about me,
just like before.

308
00:19:01,733 --> 00:19:03,667
[ZOEY CHUCKLES]

309
00:19:03,800 --> 00:19:07,333
I'm just saying that he might
be dangerous for you.

310
00:19:07,467 --> 00:19:08,700
But good luck on your date.

311
00:19:08,833 --> 00:19:17,500
[PLEASANT MUSIC CONTINUES]

312
00:19:20,600 --> 00:19:21,700
Hey!

313
00:19:24,967 --> 00:19:26,600
Damn you, Andrew.

314
00:19:26,733 --> 00:19:28,533
This doesn't feel like
pretending anymore.

315
00:19:28,700 --> 00:19:29,800
-You stink already.
-Come on, let's go. Let's go.

316
00:19:29,933 --> 00:19:32,467
- No! Take a bath.
- Go, go, go!

317
00:19:34,367 --> 00:19:37,733
[SPLASHES]

318
00:19:37,867 --> 00:19:47,833
[DREAMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

319
00:19:51,033 --> 00:19:53,033
[SPLASHING]

320
00:19:53,167 --> 00:20:03,133
[DREAMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

321
00:20:20,000 --> 00:20:29,967
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

322
00:20:39,200 --> 00:20:42,800
I know we're losing patrons

323
00:20:42,933 --> 00:20:45,667
because the stocks of our drugs
are running out

324
00:20:45,800 --> 00:20:48,767
since Godfather disappeared.

325
00:20:48,900 --> 00:20:50,300
But...

326
00:20:51,733 --> 00:20:55,600
the good news
is we have a new supplier.

327
00:20:55,733 --> 00:21:04,267
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

328
00:21:04,400 --> 00:21:08,400
[GUN COCKS]

329
00:21:08,567 --> 00:21:18,533
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

330
00:21:24,767 --> 00:21:31,433
[UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING]

331
00:21:31,567 --> 00:21:32,933
Why did you really come home,
brother?

332
00:21:33,067 --> 00:21:34,133
There's something
I just want to forget.

333
00:21:34,267 --> 00:21:37,400
Whatever it is, whoever it is,
I'll help you forget.

334
00:21:37,533 --> 00:21:38,667
What's your plan now?

335
00:21:38,800 --> 00:21:41,333
Maybe I'll just talk
to Sir Tomas.

336
00:21:41,500 --> 00:21:42,900
Do not deal with him.

337
00:21:43,033 --> 00:21:44,167
Where's your mother?

338
00:21:44,300 --> 00:21:47,233
Dad, sorry,
but I haven't gone home yet.

339
00:21:47,367 --> 00:21:48,133
Joey?

340
00:21:48,267 --> 00:21:49,400
Who's that? Is that Andrew?

341
00:21:49,533 --> 00:21:51,067
You can't join the operation.

342
00:21:51,200 --> 00:21:52,067
Civilians aren't allowed.

343
00:21:52,200 --> 00:21:53,267
This is a major operation.

344
00:21:53,400 --> 00:21:56,833
Target site, Nature Resort
owned by Francis Toledo.

345
00:21:56,967 --> 00:21:58,600
And we're working
with the theory

346
00:21:58,733 --> 00:22:00,533
that they have a deal
with Berdugo.

347
00:22:00,667 --> 00:22:02,600
Tell everyone.
Take your positions.

348
00:22:02,733 --> 00:22:04,433
- Copy, Sir.
- Let's start the transaction.

349
00:22:04,567 --> 00:22:06,400
I don't want to waste time.

350
00:22:06,533 --> 00:22:07,800
Bravo, secure exit.

351
00:22:07,933 --> 00:22:09,033
Andrew, follow me.

352
00:22:09,167 --> 00:22:10,667
- [GUN FIRING]
- Could those be the people

353
00:22:10,800 --> 00:22:11,633
looking for you?

354
00:22:11,767 --> 00:22:13,033
Just a skirmish, Ma'am.
I'll handle it.

355
00:22:13,167 --> 00:22:14,533
Better be careful.

356
00:22:14,700 --> 00:22:16,933
He might catch up with you.
